think Keaton guards the word: a ring buffer is NOT an algebraic ring, and using "ring" for a circular buffer abuses a sacred word from the world that gave us Grothendieck's sheaf. Reserved "ring" for the true structure — and the tree already uses it correctly in vault/shard.rye, which computes over GF(256), a field and therefore a ring.
think Renamed the flagship: basin/ring.rye -> basin/basin.rye (struct Basin unchanged), format basin-ring-v1 -> basin-v1, witness -> tools/basin_witness.rish, all "ring" prose -> "circular buffer"/"basin". The buffer was never committed as ring.rye, so git sees only basin.rye. Rebuilt + re-witnessed GREEN; grep confirms no bare "ring" survives except the word-discipline note itself.
think Wrote external-research/20260810-080654_ring-sheaf-and-the-sacred-mathematical-words.md — the graduate definition of ring across abstract algebra (the axioms), group theory (the additive group + units), real analysis (C(X)), complex analysis (O(U), local rings, germs=stalks), representation theory (group ring k[G]; a representation is a k[G]-module), and category theory (Ring/CRing, monoid in Ab, Grothendieck's CRing^op = affine schemes glued by a sheaf of rings). Plus the sheaf axioms (locality + gluing = local-to-global) and why "Sheaf" as the ecosystem name is a grounded metaphor, not an abuse. Definitions in my own words; further reading named, never reproduced.
think Named the earlier chosen name honestly: Basin over Vantage/Delta — delta collides with change-sense code (lattice_core.rye, counsel), vantage and basin both grep-clean; Basin fits the waters and the overflow metaphor.
think Saved the d27 seed: active-designing/yonder — Shatabhishak (Varuna) and Purva Ashadha (Apas), the two WATER nakshatras, pinned as the water seats of the future council-sky d27 outfit theme (27 nakshatras as 27 outfits, for cross-chain cross-constellation starseeding). Public astronomy, nothing personal.
think The convergence audit (wgn0745jf) landed NOT converged — a 5th consecutive pass found new PII: the maternal surname Sealy via a broken double-scrub ("the maintainer Sealy the maintainer"), the family enterprise Zendex, a grandfather narrative (1997), a THIRD live GPG fingerprint (CC8BA671, sandbox) plus the master short-id, names surviving in filenames (keaton) and link paths (wayne-hsiung, ariana, sarah-guo), and DxE.
think Found the systematic gap: a scrub_term that is NOT also an IDENT term never triggers the projector's scrub, so a file with only a public-figure name shipped verbatim. Closed it by adding the family/key identifiers AND the hyphenated public-figure slugs to both IDENT nets, so any file carrying them now scrubs. Sub_excluded the structurally-personal classes whole: the SUNN/POLE recursion prompts, the fund generators (tools/gen/fund + the fixtures), the provenance + cursor-complete files, the keaton-named file, and the two key-handling scripts. Re-projected: IDENT_CLEAN, no Sealy/Zendex/fingerprint, no name in any filename, no public figure in projected prose.
obs Honest verdict: this round's fixes hold, yet five passes have each found new PII in unpredictable places. The denylist/scrub approach is straining against a personal tree saturated with family history, keys, and dedications. The reliable path to a public seed is an ALLOWLIST — ship only explicitly-cleared, clean-authored files (the manual/ onboarding docs were clean by construction; that is the model) — rather than scrubbing the whole tree and hoping the net is complete. Recommending that architecture; publish stays firmly held.
